          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"id\":85,\"filmId\":71,\"screeningDate\":\"2026-01-20T18:30\",\"doorsTime\":\"6pm\",\"filmTime\":\"6.30pm\",\"capacity\":37,\"ticketsSold\":37,\"price\":1100,\"format\":\"Digital\",\"excludeFromGiftVouchers\":false,\"film\":{\"id\":71,\"title\":\"BEYOND THE INFINITE TWO MINUTES\",\"description\":\"In a small café, a seemingly ordinary television reveals a glimpse of the future: exactly two minutes ahead. The café owner and his friends experiment with this time loop, only for simple curiosity to cascade into chaos, comedy, and escalating temporal confusion. Beyond the Infinite Two Minutes transforms a low-stakes premise into a labyrinth of cause and effect, where every action multiplies and timelines overlap in unexpected ways.\\n\\nYamaguchi’s long-take cinematography and meticulous real-time framing create a kinetic, immersive experience, trapping characters—and viewers—in the cascading logic of near-future sight. What begins as a playful experiment becomes a study of consequence, improvisation, and human desire to control the uncontrollable. Time here is both a tool and a trap, and connection feels urgent, fleeting, and perpetually one step ahead of itself.\",\"runtime\":87,\"year\":2020,\"country\":\"Japan\",\"director\":\"Junta Yamaguchi\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://thatshelf.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/BEYOND-THE-INFINITE-2-MINUTES.jpg\",\"imageCropX\":50,\"imageCropY\":50,\"ageCertificate\":\"12\"}}",
