            "text": "{\"id\":65,\"filmId\":38,\"screeningDate\":\"2026-01-23T18:30\",\"doorsTime\":\"6pm\",\"filmTime\":\"6.30pm\",\"capacity\":37,\"ticketsSold\":36,\"price\":1100,\"format\":\"Digital\",\"excludeFromGiftVouchers\":false,\"film\":{\"id\":38,\"title\":\"DANCE FREAK + VIDEO INTRO\",\"description\":\"On the worst day of his life, an unassuming man crosses paths with a feral, hypnotic stranger who looks exactly like him. The encounter detonates his reality: violence erupts, memories collapse, and he wakes days later implicated in crimes he doesn’t understand. As his identity splinters and the city turns hostile, the question isn’t how to clear his name, but whether he can prove he’s even himself.\\n\\nCo-directed by Alan Resnick and Robby Rackleff, Dance Freak is a low-budget, high-intensity descent into psychological chaos. Blending abrasive humor, stark black-and-white imagery, and a relentless audiovisual assault, the film channels their shared lineage of unsettling genre work into something lean, volatile, and deliberately unhinged.\",\"runtime\":90,\"year\":2025,\"country\":\"USA\",\"director\":\"Alan Resnick, Robby Rackleff\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://newnextfilmfest.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Dance-Freak-NEWNEXT_1_resize.jpg\",\"imageCropX\":50,\"imageCropY\":50,\"ageCertificate\":\"18\"}}",
            "size": 1250
