          "headersSize": 697,
          "cookies": [],
          "redirectURL": "",
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"id\":68,\"filmId\":56,\"screeningDate\":\"2026-01-24T18:15\",\"doorsTime\":\"5.45pm\",\"filmTime\":\"6.15pm\",\"capacity\":37,\"ticketsSold\":33,\"price\":1100,\"format\":\"Digital\",\"excludeFromGiftVouchers\":false,\"film\":{\"id\":56,\"title\":\"PRIME CUT\",\"description\":\"A seasoned mob enforcer is sent from Chicago to rural Missouri to settle a dispute with a sadistic meatpacking boss whose criminal empire runs as brutally as his slaughterhouses. As the job spirals into a collision of organised crime, forced labour, and industrial violence, the boundaries between urban professionalism and pastoral brutality collapse. Hard-edged and deeply unsettling, Michael Ritchie’s Prime Cut exposes an America where exploitation is systemic and bodies are commodities, blending crime thriller conventions with a bleak, often surreal vision of power, corruption, and survival on the margins.\",\"runtime\":88,\"year\":1972,\"country\":\"USA\",\"director\":\"Michael Ritchie\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://quadcinema.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/05/Prime-Cut-1400x619.jpg\",\"imageCropX\":50,\"imageCropY\":50,\"ageCertificate\":\"18\"}}",
