          "cookies": [],
          "redirectURL": "",
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"id\":69,\"filmId\":57,\"screeningDate\":\"2026-01-25T15:30\",\"doorsTime\":\"3pm\",\"filmTime\":\"3.30pm\",\"capacity\":37,\"ticketsSold\":37,\"price\":1100,\"format\":\"Digital\",\"excludeFromGiftVouchers\":false,\"film\":{\"id\":57,\"title\":\"HARD TO BE A GOD\",\"description\":\"A group of scientists observe a distant planet locked in a perpetual medieval state, where brutality, ignorance, and superstition dominate everyday life. Disguised as nobles and forbidden to intervene, one emissary moves through a world of mud, violence, and oppression, increasingly consumed by the moral cost of detachment. Monumental, abrasive, and relentlessly immersive, Aleksei German’s Hard to Be a God dismantles the conventions of science fiction, using historical grotesquerie to interrogate power, responsibility, and the limits of enlightenment in the face of human cruelty.\",\"runtime\":177,\"year\":2013,\"country\":\"Russia/Germany\",\"director\":\"Aleksei German\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://newcityfilm.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/05/Hard-to-be-a-god.jpg\",\"imageCropX\":0,\"imageCropY\":50,\"ageCertificate\":\"18\"}}",
