            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"id\":70,\"filmId\":58,\"screeningDate\":\"2026-01-25T19:30\",\"doorsTime\":\"7pm\",\"filmTime\":\"7.30pm\",\"capacity\":37,\"ticketsSold\":37,\"price\":1100,\"format\":\"Digital\",\"excludeFromGiftVouchers\":false,\"film\":{\"id\":58,\"title\":\"CHRISTIANE F.\",\"description\":\"A thirteen-year-old girl drifts from adolescent boredom into the underground world of drugs, prostitution, and petty crime that surrounds Berlin’s Bahnhof Zoo. What begins as experimentation quickly hardens into dependency, as friendships, family structures, and any sense of safety erode under the pressures of addiction. Stark, unsentimental, and closely rooted in lived testimony, Uli Edel’s Christiane F. documents youth culture at the point of collapse, presenting a bleak social landscape shaped by neglect, urban anonymity, and the quiet brutality of survival at the margins.\",\"runtime\":131,\"year\":1981,\"country\":\"Germany\",\"director\":\"Uli Edel\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/janus_stills/6740-/28912id_095_0004_28912id_126_w1600.jpg\",\"imageCropX\":50,\"imageCropY\":50,\"ageCertificate\":\"18\"}}",
