          "cookies": [],
          "redirectURL": "",
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"id\":80,\"filmId\":65,\"screeningDate\":\"2026-01-30T18:30\",\"doorsTime\":\"6pm\",\"filmTime\":\"6.30pm\",\"capacity\":34,\"ticketsSold\":20,\"price\":1100,\"format\":\"Digital\",\"excludeFromGiftVouchers\":false,\"film\":{\"id\":65,\"title\":\"SCANNERS INC. PRESENTS: KILLING ZOE\",\"description\":\"In the suffocating heat of Paris, an American safecracker is drawn into a botched bank robbery that spirals into nihilistic excess, chemical detachment, and self-annihilation. Killing Zoe captures the early-90s collision of cinephilia and disaffection: a film obsessed with its own cool, yet unable to escape the violence and emptiness it performs. Avary stages crime as a closed circuit of bravado and decay, where loyalty erodes under narcotics and adrenaline, and style becomes a form of denial rather than control.\\n\\nThis screening is presented by Scanners, Inc. from a 35mm scan overseen by Peter Aldanmaz (aka NC-17), responsible for the film’s recent restoration. Drawn from release prints, the scan preserves the texture of the original theatrical experience—grain intact, reel-change marks visible, and damage left unpolished.\",\"runtime\":96,\"year\":1993,\"country\":\"USA\",\"director\":\"Roger Avary\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4DBc!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fdd9603c0-b686-400a-8ec5-24e7a0ea1199_1280x688.jpeg\",\"imageCropX\":50,\"imageCropY\":50,\"ageCertificate\":\"18\"}}",
