          "cookies": [],
          "redirectURL": "",
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"id\":81,\"filmId\":66,\"screeningDate\":\"2026-01-30T20:45\",\"doorsTime\":\"8.15pm\",\"filmTime\":\"8.45pm\",\"capacity\":34,\"ticketsSold\":31,\"price\":1100,\"format\":\"Digital\",\"excludeFromGiftVouchers\":false,\"film\":{\"id\":66,\"title\":\"SCANNERS INC. PRESENTS: THE RULES OF ATTRACTION\",\"description\":\"Set within the insulated sprawl of an East Coast liberal arts college, The Rules of Attraction fractures youth into overlapping monologues of desire, resentment, and emotional vacancy. Characters orbit one another without alignment, mistaking proximity for intimacy and indulgence for meaning. Avary adapts Bret Easton Ellis with a cold formalism that mirrors the film’s worldview: time loops, perspectives contradict, and events recur without consequence. Romance is transactional, sex is anesthetic, and connection is endlessly deferred. What emerges is not a cautionary tale but a system—self-contained, performative, and quietly brutal—where everyone is both observer and casualty.\\n\\nThis screening is presented by Scanners, Inc. from a 35mm scan.\",\"runtime\":110,\"year\":2002,\"country\":\"USA\",\"director\":\"Roger Avary\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://images.mubicdn.net/images/film/14708/cache-50923-1745491083/image-w1280.jpg\",\"imageCropX\":50,\"imageCropY\":50,\"ageCertificate\":\"18\"}}",
