          "headersSize": 697,
          "cookies": [],
          "redirectURL": "",
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"id\":82,\"filmId\":68,\"screeningDate\":\"2026-01-31T15:30\",\"doorsTime\":\"3pm\",\"filmTime\":\"3.30pm\",\"capacity\":34,\"ticketsSold\":8,\"price\":1100,\"format\":\"Digital\",\"excludeFromGiftVouchers\":false,\"film\":{\"id\":68,\"title\":\"SCANNERS INC. PRESENTS: OUT FOR JUSTICE\",\"description\":\"On the streets of Brooklyn, a cop’s pursuit of a psychopath who murdered his partner escalates into a one-man campaign of humiliation, intimidation, and retributive violence. Out for Justice strips the police thriller down to its rawest components: territorial masculinity, public dominance, and justice reduced to spectacle. Steven Seagal’s Gino Felino operates less as a lawman than as an unstoppable corrective force, moving through bars, alleys, and family spaces with absolute certainty and zero moral hesitation.\\n\\nFlynn frames the city as a hostile arena where order is imposed, not negotiated, and where legality is secondary to personal codes of loyalty and honour. The film’s notorious confrontations—played out in full view of the community—transform justice into a performance designed to shame as much as punish. Devoid of irony or self-reflection, Out for Justice embodies a particular early-90s fantasy of control: blunt, territorial, and brutally efficient, offering catharsis not through resolution, but through dominance asserted until resistance collapses.\\n\\nThis screening is presented by Scanners, Inc. from a 35mm scan.\",\"runtime\":91,\"year\":1989,\"country\":\"USA\",\"director\":\"John Flynn\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://play-lh.googleusercontent.com/proxy/UQ0Sfg4o-p1lKrjrXauQwvhRbkEYHO7iEGEZ93aJcP4hRGN-DBUHBDDWW71l8hQfEpE-WWGXcxsDlt_DNbT688h1U4eo3tvv4OFdnrZ3yrrp_4U=s1920-w1920-h1080\",\"imageCropX\":50,\"imageCropY\":50,\"ageCertificate\":\"18\"}}",
