          "headersSize": 697,
          "cookies": [],
          "redirectURL": "",
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"id\":93,\"filmId\":35,\"screeningDate\":\"2026-02-02T21:10\",\"doorsTime\":\"8.40pm\",\"filmTime\":\"9.10pm\",\"capacity\":35,\"ticketsSold\":0,\"price\":1100,\"format\":\"Digital\",\"excludeFromGiftVouchers\":false,\"film\":{\"id\":35,\"title\":\"SHRIME TIME: A NIGHT OF BIZARRO UNDERSEEN ANIME\",\"description\":\"From radical student animation collectives to sun-bleached techno-dystopias and gore-drenched horror, Shrime Time shines where the sun daren’t: revealing the backside of seldom-seen Japanese visual culture. Expect screenings from the 1960s to the present day, paired with special guests: musicians, artists, researchers and those obsessed with the outermost edges of Japan’s visual imagination.\\n\\nThe Shirime a y?kai (Japanese folkloric spirit and the evenings conveniently misspelled namesake) whose sole purpose is to startle unsuspecting samurai by revealing an eyeball in place of an arsehole. In his sick, twisted way, Shirime embodies the very spirit of B-cinema - a flash of grotesque brilliance, whose origin and intent remain a mystery, leaving the path forever altered.\\n\\nSo come. Sit still in the dark. Let the rectacular eye stare deep into your curious soul.\\n\\nThe Shirime is watching.\",\"runtime\":null,\"year\":null,\"country\":\"Japan\",\"director\":\"?\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://ticketlab.co.uk/index.php/uploads/37428/Screenshot-2025-08-19-at-11_35806-760x0.png\",\"imageCropX\":50,\"imageCropY\":50,\"ageCertificate\":\"18\"}}",
