          "headersSize": 697,
          "cookies": [],
          "redirectURL": "",
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"id\":120,\"filmId\":97,\"screeningDate\":\"2026-02-15T19:30\",\"doorsTime\":\"7pm\",\"filmTime\":\"7:30pm\",\"capacity\":37,\"ticketsSold\":1,\"price\":1100,\"format\":\"Digital\",\"excludeFromGiftVouchers\":false,\"film\":{\"id\":97,\"title\":\"DEATH RIDES A HORSE\",\"description\":\"As a child, Bill Meceita witnesses the massacre of his family at the hands of four outlaws, each marked by a distinctive trait burned into his memory. Years later, now an expert gunman, he sets out on a methodical hunt for those responsible. His vengeance becomes entangled with that of Ryan, an ageing gunslinger freshly released from prison and harbouring his own grievances against the same men. Their uneasy alliance — part mentorship, part rivalry — unfolds across a frontier shaped by shifting loyalties and buried histories.\\n\\nA standout of the late-1960s Italian western cycle, Death Rides a Horse combines Petroni’s precise staging with an unusually introspective approach to revenge. Ennio Morricone’s propulsive score and Carlo Carlini’s spare, expressive cinematography heighten the film’s interplay between ritualised violence and moral ambiguity. The result is a taut, atmospheric reworking of genre conventions, where vengeance is less a path to justice than a circular reckoning with the past.\",\"runtime\":114,\"year\":1967,\"country\":\"Italy/Spain\",\"director\":\"Giulio Petroni\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcRgezpty9W9dDsvzN3sSPY7vly4fJLyo1QaNQ&s\",\"imageCropX\":50,\"imageCropY\":75,\"ageCertificate\":\"15\"}}",
